Significant global pests of cotton include various species of [ bollworm
](/wiki/Bollworm "Bollworm") , such as _[ Pectinophora gossypiella
](/wiki/Pectinophora_gossypiella "Pectinophora gossypiella") _ . Sucking pests
include [ cotton stainers ](/wiki/Dysdercus "Dysdercus") , the chili thrips,
_[ Scirtothrips dorsalis ](/wiki/Scirtothrips_dorsalis "Scirtothrips
dorsalis") _ ; the cotton seed bug, _[ Oxycarenus hyalinipennis
](/wiki/Oxycarenus_hyalinipennis "Oxycarenus hyalinipennis") _ . Defoliators
include the fall armyworm, _[ Spodoptera frugiperda
](/wiki/Spodoptera_frugiperda "Spodoptera frugiperda") _ .

Cotton yield is threatened by the evolution [ of new biotypes of insects
](/wiki/Pest_evolution "Pest evolution") and [ of new pathogens
](/wiki/Crop_pathogen_evolution "Crop pathogen evolution") .  [84]
Maintaining good yield requires strategies to slow these adversaries'
evolution.  [84]

